# Keep the working tree byte-stable on every platform.
#
# Repository text is stored and checked out with LF. That is deliberate: shell
# scripts must stay runnable and the packager (scripts/package_windows.py) is the
# single place that converts the Windows script assets to CRLF inside the archive.
# Letting git normalise line endings per checkout would move that decision out of
# the build and make the shipped bytes depend on a developer's git config.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=lf
*.cs text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
